        "original_id": "546dcb1a-2466-5517-8923-bbfafb6cb321",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Maine Democratic Presidential Caucuses, 2008\n- Places: Maine, Maine's two congressional districts\n- Topics: Delegates, United States House of Representatives\n\nFacts:\n- The Maine Democratic Presidential Caucuses took place on February 10, 2008.\n- The 2008 Maine Democratic Presidential Caucuses had 24 delegates at stake.\n- Maine is divided into two congressional districts.\n- Each of Maine's congressional districts is represented by an elected member of the United States House of Representatives.\n- In the 2008 Maine Democratic Presidential Caucuses, the winner in each of Maine's two congressional districts received all of that district's delegates.\n- Maine's two congressional districts together accounted for 16 delegates in the 2008 Maine Democratic Presidential Caucuses.",
